6 Secret redaction
******************

Because AI coding agents frequently see or handle secrets, their
conversation logs can contain API keys, tokens, and other credentials in
plain text.  The optional ‘agent-log-redact’ module scans each rendered
entry for known secret formats and replaces every match with a
deterministic placeholder of the form ‘[REDACTED:LABEL:HASH8]’, where
‘HASH8’ is the first 8 hex chars of ‘sha256(secret + salt)’.  The same
secret always produces the same placeholder, so you can still reason
about which credential appears where without exposing its value.

   Enable it by loading the module:

     (require 'agent-log-redact)

   After enabling for the first time, run ‘agent-log-redact-rebuild-all’
to re-render any previously-rendered logs through the redactor.

* Menu:

* Coverage::
* Integration::
