9.1 No sessions found
=====================

Ensure that ‘agent-log-directory’ points to the correct configuration
directory (*note Directory configuration::).  The package reads
‘history.jsonl’ in that directory and looks for session files under
‘projects/’.


File: agent-log.info,  Node: Rendered files not updating,  Next: Live updates not working,  Prev: No sessions found,  Up: Troubleshooting

9.2 Rendered files not updating
===============================

If a rendered file appears stale, press ‘g’ (‘agent-log-refresh’) in the
buffer to force a full re-render (*note Sync and rendering::).  You can
also delete the index file (‘_index.el’ in the rendered directory) to
force re-rendering of all ordinary sessions on next access.


File: agent-log.info,  Node: Live updates not working,  Prev: Rendered files not updating,  Up: Troubleshooting

9.3 Live updates not working
============================

Verify that ‘agent-log-live-update’ is set to ‘t’ (*note Live
updates::).  Live updates rely on ‘file-notify’, which requires OS-level
file watching support.  On some systems (e.g., remote filesystems via
TRAMP), file notifications may not be available.


